<script module>
  import Demo from "$ui/components/Demo.abide"
  import CounterCacheDemo from "$ui/demos/caching/CounterCacheDemo.abide"
  import CacheFalseDemo from "$ui/demos/caching/CacheFalseDemo.abide"
  import MetricDemo from "$ui/demos/caching/MetricDemo.abide"
  import AmendDemo from "$ui/demos/caching/AmendDemo.abide"
  import SharedDemo from "$ui/demos/caching/SharedDemo.abide"
  import TtlDemo from "$ui/demos/caching/TtlDemo.abide"
</script>

<main class="page">
  <h1>Cache verbs</h1>
  <p class="lead">A read is a memoized <a href="/caching/cell">cell</a> slot: reuse it, <code>refresh</code> it over the stale value, <code>invalidate</code> it to force a lazy re-fetch, <code>amend</code> it in place. This page is the verbs and the cache behaviour (partial match, <code>shared</code>, <code>ttl</code>); the reactive <a href="/caching/probes">probes</a> and the <a href="/caching/global">global</a> tag selectors have their own pages. Every demo below drives a real RPC (in-process on the server, a fetch from the browser).</p>

  <p>The server counts how many times the handler actually ran. Read again and again — the count <strong>holds</strong> because the slot is reused. <code>invalidate</code> drops the slot, so the next read re-fetches and the count <strong>climbs</strong>.</p>
  <Demo id="counter" title="Cached read is reused (call count holds)" server="src/server/rpc/cacheCounter.ts" client="src/ui/demos/caching/CounterCacheDemo.abide" tab="server">
    <CounterCacheDemo />
  </Demo>

  <p>The opposite of the default: <code>cache: false</code> opts a call OUT of the cell entirely — every call runs, on both sides (no retain, no coalesced reuse, no client cache). Read both below: the <code>cache: false</code> counter <strong>climbs</strong> on every read while the default cached one <strong>holds</strong>. (A <code>cache: false</code> mutation is the same — every call runs, at-least-once; a <code>FormData</code> body always bypasses too, since it can't be cache-keyed.)</p>
  <Demo id="cache-false" title="<code>cache: false</code> — every call runs" server="src/server/rpc/cacheOff.ts" client="src/ui/demos/caching/CacheFalseDemo.abide" tab="server">
    <CacheFalseDemo />
  </Demo>

  <p>Slots are keyed by the <em>whole</em> args object. Load all three slots, then invalidate the partial selector <code>{'{'} team: "red" {'}'}</code> — it matches every superset slot, so both <strong>red</strong> slots re-fetch (their run counts climb together) while <strong>blue</strong> is untouched.</p>
  <Demo id="metric" title="invalidate — partial-object match" server="src/server/rpc/cacheMetric.ts" client="src/ui/demos/caching/MetricDemo.abide" tab="server">
    <MetricDemo />
  </Demo>

  <p>Load once (the server run count is small), then <code>amend</code> the slot value in place. Value-form sets it to <code>999</code>; updater-form derives the next value from the current — both are local, so the handler never re-runs and no fetch happens.</p>
  <Demo id="amend" title="<code>amend(args, value | updater)</code> — mutate in place, no re-fetch" server="src/server/rpc/cacheCounter.ts" client="src/ui/demos/caching/AmendDemo.abide" tab="server">
    <AmendDemo />
  </Demo>

  <p>A <code>shared</code> read's slot is process-global. Each <code>raw()</code> is a separate request: the shared read returns the <strong>same</strong> run count both times (one handler run served both), while a per-request (non-shared) read re-runs and <strong>climbs</strong>. The shared handler is identity-independent and fail-closed.</p>
  <Demo id="shared" title="<code>cache: {'{'} shared: true {'}'}</code> — cross-request cache" server="src/server/rpc/cacheShared.ts" client="src/ui/demos/caching/SharedDemo.abide" tab="server">
    <SharedDemo />
  </Demo>

  <p>A shared read with a 700ms TTL. Two reads inside the window return the same count (served from cache); after the window elapses the next read re-runs the handler and the count climbs.</p>
  <Demo id="ttl" title="<code>cache: {'{'} ttl {'}'}</code> — the slot expires + re-fetches" server="src/server/rpc/cacheTtl.ts" client="src/ui/demos/caching/TtlDemo.abide" tab="server">
    <TtlDemo />
  </Demo>
</main>
